  "answer": "The bug is clear: `total` subtracts each amount (`sum -= entry.amount`) instead of adding. Fixing it while keeping the exported shape:\nFixed and verified. Summary:\n\n**The fix** — `src/ledger.ts`, one line: the running total subtracted each entry's amount (`sum -= entry.amount`), so `[{amount: 4}, {amount: 6}]` produced `-10`. Changed the operator to `sum += entry.amount` so every entry adds to the total.\n\n**Preserved** — the exported shape (`interface Entry`, `function total`) and `test/oracle.test.ts` are untouched, per project instructions.\n\n**Test run** — `bun test`: 1 pass, 0 fail (3 assertions), covering positive sums (`4 + 6 = 10`), the empty-ledger case (`0`), and negative amounts (`-3` passes through correctly)."
